      "writtenOn": "2022-05-16T20:36:14Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "You\u0027ll probably need to add support for `ctx.Config().AllowMissingDependencies \u003d\u003d true` here so that parsing a `gen_notices` modules in a partial manifest that is missing it\u0027s `for` modules doesn\u0027t fail parsing the Android.bp files but does cause the rules for the `gen_notices` file to exit with an error if built.  That\u0027s usually handled automatically when you add a missing dependency through the normal dependency functions or call `ctx.AddMissingDependencies` to add one, but it works by overwriting the module\u0027s rules, and this module doesn\u0027t have any rules because they are in the singleton, so you\u0027ll probably have to manually create an `android.ErrorRule`.",
      "revId": "5db7e0d4435bcc8e163dfeb70343f1596f650395",
